<INFO> Unsafe `tx.origin` Identified.

VULNERABILITY NAME: Reliance on `tx.origin` for Authorization
'''
DETAILED DESCRIPTION: The `changeOwner` function uses `tx.origin` to verify that the caller is the contract owner. This is unsafe because `tx.origin` represents the original externally owned account (EOA) that initiated the transaction, not the immediate caller (which could be a malicious contract). If a legitimate user (owner) interacts with a malicious contract, that malicious contract can call `changeOwner` on behalf of the owner, bypassing the intended access control. This allows an attacker to change the owner of the Vault contract to their own address, gaining full control.

